This patch is needed because Chromium's Linux non-clang archive branch assumes
GNU thin-archive behavior that does not match Solaris archiver support.

What it does:
- keeps the Linux thin-archive branch from firing on Solaris targets

Why it is needed:
- without it, the build tries to use a Linux archive path that Solaris ar does
  not support

--- a/v8-147.4.0/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/v8-147.4.0/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -2608,7 +2608,7 @@
 # 2. Remove the thin_archive config, so that the .a file actually contains all
 #    .o files, instead of just references to .o files in the build directoy
 config("thin_archive") {
-  if ((is_apple && use_lld) || (is_linux && !is_clang) || current_os == "aix") {
+  if ((is_apple && use_lld) || (is_linux && current_os != "solaris" && !is_clang) || current_os == "aix") {
     # The macOS and iOS linker ld64.ldd doesn't support thin archive without
     # symbol table, gcc on linux also throws the error `archive has no index`.
     # AIX does support -s option, not -S option.
